   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "4, 5 and 6 Trinity Street (Caius-owned, Victorian Gothic): red/brown diaper-pattern brick, windows in heavy black-painted stepped surrounds, white 2-light sashes, iron balconettes on no.4 1st floor, stone quoins at S end; three steep gables with white fretted bargeboards and attic windows (modelled as small windows below eave). Ground: grey-green canopied 'cambridge contemporary art' gallery front (nos.5-6, N), green panelled house door, mint-green 'GILES & Co' shopfront (no.4, S). No shop tags in OSM; names from photos. x positions estimated from an oblique photo."
  },
